/**
 * The `rx` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property defines the x-axis, or
 * horizontal, radius of an SVG `ellipse` and the horizontal curve of the corners of an SVG `rect`
 * rectangle. If present, it overrides the shape's `rx` attribute.
 *
 * Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
 * Percentages: refer to the width of the current SVG viewport.
 *
 * Keyword effects:
 * - auto: When set or defaulting to `auto`, the `rx` value equals the absolute length value used
 * for `ry`. If both `rx` and `ry` have a computed value of `auto`, the used value is `0`.
 *
 * Grammar: <length-percentage> | auto
